(FIL-78: all three documented catchable error classes are catchable: out-of-bounds list access, out-of-bounds buffer access, fixed buffer overflow, and file operation failure.
 Also covers: FIL-77, FIL-79, FIL-80.
 Run from the vox-fuzz worktree root; the probe creates everything it
 needs under vf_scratch/files/ and touches nothing else.
 Ran: VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox docs/ledger/probes/files/FIL-78.vox -o p && ./p
 actual output:
   out-of-bounds list access is catchable
   out-of-bounds buffer access is catchable
   fixed buffer overflow is catchable
   a file operation failure is catchable
)
Create a directory called "vf_scratch".
Create a directory called "vf_scratch/files".
open a file for writing called seedfile at "vf_scratch/files/lines.txt".
Write "alpha\nbeta\ngamma\n" to seedfile.
Close seedfile.
(1. out-of-bounds list access)
a list called items is [1, 2, 3].
a number called 'the out of range item' is element 100 of items.
On error print "out-of-bounds list access is catchable".
(2. out-of-bounds buffer access)
a buffer called small is 8 bytes in size.
append "ABCD" to small.
a number called 'the out of range byte' is byte 100 of small.
On error print "out-of-bounds buffer access is catchable".
(3. fixed buffer overflow)
open a file for reading called source at "vf_scratch/files/lines.txt".
Read from source into small.
On error print "fixed buffer overflow is catchable".
Close source.
(4. file operation failure)
open a file for reading called missing at "vf_scratch/files/absent.txt".
On error print "a file operation failure is catchable".
